<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Close of play scores on the</p>
<p>second day of four-day English County Championship cricket</p>
<p>matches on Friday:</p>
<p>At Cardiff: Glamorgan 281. Middlesex 251-5 (J.Kallis 96,</p>
<p>M.Ramprakash 63).</p>
<p>At The Oval: Surrey 549 (A.Stewart 271 not out). Yorkshire</p>
<p>226-4 (D.Lehmann 61 not out, D.Byas 59, M.Moxon 57).</p>
<p>At Bristol: Worcestershire 250 (S.Lampitt 52; M.Alleyne</p>
<p>5-41) and 36-0. Gloucestershire 229.</p>
<p>At Edgbaston: Derbyshire 200. Warwickshire 209-3 (A.Moles</p>
<p>83, D.Hemp 60).</p>
<p>At Old Trafford: Kent 373 (B.Phillips 100 not out, A.Wells</p>
<p>65). Lancashire 113-5.</p>
<p>At Basingstoke: Hampshire 204 and 189 (M.Hayden 63; G.Rose</p>
<p>5-53). Somerset 159 (P.Holloway 73 not out; K.James 5-44).</p>
<p>At Hove: Sussex 140 and 220-5 (R.Rao 89, N.Lenham 60). Essex</p>
<p>384 (R.Irani 110, R.Rollins 82).</p>
</text>
